      "id": "luckycam_identity",
      "question": "What is LuckyCam?",
      "answer": "LuckyCam is a camera system that can operate as a normal direct imaging system, despite being primarily used in service mode. It consists of an array of four electron-multiplying (photon-counting) CCDs in a line, providing a contiguous imaging area of 4000 x 1000 pixels. The system includes real-time image display, allowing users to observe the image building up on the screen. [D-370df38cd647c4e7-C1]",
